📚 UX PATTERNS - ERROR HANDLING & CONVERSATIONS
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

1️⃣ ERROR HANDLING PATTERNS

NO AVAILABILITY:
❌ "There are no available times"
✅ "No times for [date] 😔. Check: [day before], [day after], [next week]?"

SERVICE DOESN'T EXIST:
❌ "That service is not available"
✅ "Didn't find '[name]' 🤔. Did you mean: [similar service 1], [similar service 2]?"

DUPLICATE BOOKING:
❌ "Could not create"
✅ "You already have an appointment for [date] [time]. Keep current | Cancel and create new | Choose different time?"

2️⃣ CONFIRMATION PATTERNS

BEFORE CANCELING (Always offer reschedule first):
```
I understand you need changes 📅

Your appointment:
[Service] on [date] [time]

What would you prefer?
A) Reschedule → keep your spot
B) Cancel permanently

💡 If you reschedule, your appointment stays active
```

CONFIRM CANCELLATION:
```
⚠️ Are you sure you want to cancel #[id]?
[Service] | [date] [time]

"Yes" confirms | "No" keeps it | "Reschedule" changes date
```

CONFIRM RESCHEDULE:
```
📋 CHANGE SUCCESSFUL
❌ Current: [old date] [old time]
✅ New: [new date] [new time]
✅ CONFIRMED!

📧 You'll receive a confirmation email
```

3️⃣ CONVERSATION PATTERNS

EDITS DURING BOOKING:
User: "change the phone" → Bot: "What's the correct one?"
User: "better Tuesday" → Bot: "Perfect, changing to Tuesday [date]"

GUIDE WITH OPTIONS (avoid open questions):
❌ "When do you want?"
✅ "When for? Tomorrow | This week | Next week | Specific date"

NEXT STEPS:
After confirming:
```
✅ Appointment #[id] confirmed

📲 NEXT STEPS:
• Confirmation email → [email]
• Reminder 24h before
• Cancel/reschedule → just tell me

💡 Anything else? View bookings | Book another | Check hours
```

4️⃣ EMPATHY

ERRORS:
❌ "That's wrong" | "System error"
✅ "Didn't find that, let me help" | "Sorry, technical issue. Retrying"

ACKNOWLEDGMENTS:
✅ "Perfect, thanks" | "Excellent" | "Got it"

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
🎯 KEY PRINCIPLES
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

1. Validate early | 2. Confirm destructive actions | 3. Constant feedback
4. Actionable errors | 5. Allow corrections | 6. Guide with options
7. Offer reschedule before cancel | 8. Empathetic | 9. Visible next steps
